# Normalise line endings, so a fresh clone behaves the same on every platform.
#
# This is not housekeeping. Several tests read repository documents and parse
# them - the service catalogue is checked against the observed enrollment form
# in research/utility-connect-route-audit.md rather than against a hardcoded
# copy, because a hardcoded copy would agree with itself forever and prove
# nothing. Those parsers look for `\n\n`, and a Windows checkout hands them
# `\r\n\r\n`.
#
# The result was that `npm run verify`, the first instruction in the README,
# failed with two red tests on a fresh Windows clone and passed everywhere else.
# A reviewer would have had no way to tell that from a real regression.
#
# Everything git recognises as text is stored and checked out with LF. The
# binary types are listed explicitly so nothing tries to "fix" their contents.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
